                <pb facs="1224" n="966" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg966"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1627</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>648. Your 629, March 12, 5 p. m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1366-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    note received to-day, replies that as conditions of the eventual occupation of
                    Constantinople as result of present operations in Dardanelles depend essentially
                    upon the events of war and cannot be determined in advance, it is impossible for
                    French Government to accept proposal in question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
